{"name":"Blithe","hex":"#0099d1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blithe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A river in Staffordshire, England, which joins the River Trent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blithe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Albert Blithe","blocks":[{"text":"Albert Blithe was an American career soldier who served as a private first class with Easy Company, 2nd Battalion, 506th Parachute Infantry Regiment, in the 101st Airborne Division during World War II. He served again with the Airborne during the Korean War and was twice decorated for gallantry. He eventually rose to the rank of Master Sergeant in the Army. His life story was featured in the 2010 book A Company of Heroes: Personal Memories about the Real Band of Brothers and the Legacy They Left Us by Marcus Brotherton."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a5/Sgt_Blithe_at_Toccoa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_Blithe","wikidata":"Q483934"},{"title":"John Blithe (MP)","blocks":[{"text":"John Blithe of Wells, Somerset, was an English politician."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Blithe_(MP)","wikidata":"Q22336769"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Sgt_Blithe_at_Toccoa.jpg/250px-Sgt_Blithe_at_Toccoa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a5/Sgt_Blithe_at_Toccoa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Sgt_Blithe_at_Toccoa.jpg/250px-Sgt_Blithe_at_Toccoa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlithetoccoa.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Hinge on blue dumpster","image":"https://thumb